# The layers that deny having a remainder at all. One row per layer filing the second branch of
# the `StatedRemainder` wrapper: a typed reason there is no remainder, and the note that argues for
# it.
#
# The model contradicted in its own format
#   This is what the wrapper is for. The model claims every layer has a remainder. Requiring the
#   wrapper makes a sender who disagrees say so explicitly rather than leave a field empty. Every
#   row here is somebody using that right.
#
# Why this arm is a `ClaimAbsence`
#   The right is narrower than it looks. "There is no remainder" reads two ways: nothing to
#   subtract from, or the difference is zero. Only the first is a blank. A difference of zero is a
#   clearance (`Fit` settles the line-to-line case in prose, "minimum clearance is zero"), carrying
#   a quantity of 0, 0 and 0 and a sign, and a blank throws the sign away. So `none` cannot be
#   spelled here, and a layer that means "the two coincide exactly" files the clearance.
#
# Why the note is carried
#   Read without its note, a denial looks like five NULLs (sign, absorber and quantity all blank),
#   which is exactly the shape of a document that said nothing. One of the notes says so in as many
#   words: "filed as a counter-example ... not as a gap in this document". A gap is what that
#   reading stores. The note is carried because keeping only the reason keeps the fact and loses
#   the argument.
#
# Run this alone and read the notes
#   The notes in the corpus say the same thing in different words: this layer states no nameplate,
#   so there is nothing to subtract the demand from, and the question has no meaning rather than an
#   answer of nothing. None may say "a supply with no quantum divides exactly", which is a different
#   claim and a false one: with no quantum there is no residue (layers/decomposed.sqlc), and the
#   nameplate less the demand still stands. Let the notes disagree with the structure, and the rule
#   downstream prints the right reason ("no nameplate is stated") beside the wrong one.
-- pm:Layer/pm:remainder taking the pm:absent branch of pm:StatedRemainder.
SELECT l.filing, l.layer,
       l.remainder_absent      AS reason,
       l.remainder_absent_note AS argument
FROM pm.layer l
WHERE l.remainder_absent IS NOT NULL
